{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1465632-folk-magic","id":1465632,"title":"Folk magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-28T06:19:07-07:00","id":1465632,"title":"Folk magic","content":"I am running a folk-horror style game where bad things happen to strangers and the villagers have a long list of superstitions. Everybody knows verbal charms and carries amulets; salt and herbs line windows, owl skulls hang from porches. <br /> <br /> While it isn\u2019t strictly necessary \u2013 the players are more about story than system \u2013 I would like to have some system for the protective qualities of these common measures used by folks with no specialized magical talent but merely common cultural wisdom. When a vampire tries to climb in the window, when a witch throws a hex, or when a fae glamours the cliff to look like a path... automatic contest of wills? A dot of Supernatural Resistance? Something else?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T06:25:51-07:00","id":1465637,"title":"","content":"Clash of Wills where the mortals roll Attribute + Trinket\u2019s Dot Rating? <br /> <br /> Abjuration/Warding/Binding rules for ephemeral entities expanded to generic monsters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T06:34:01-07:00","id":1465639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1465632-folk-magic#post1465632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am running a folk-horror style game where bad things happen to strangers and the villagers have a long list of superstitions. Everybody knows verbal charms and carries amulets; salt and herbs line windows, owl skulls hang from porches. <br /> <br /> While it isn\u2019t strictly necessary \u2013 the players are more about story than system \u2013 I would like to have some system for the protective qualities of these common measures used by folks with no specialized magical talent but merely common cultural wisdom. When a vampire tries to climb in the window, when a witch throws a hex, or when a fae glamours the cliff to look like a path... automatic contest of wills? A dot of Supernatural Resistance? Something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can find good rules about using those charms on core book of Chronicle of darkness.<br /> Occult skill is all that you need, and it works well while exploiting the Bans and Banes of ephemeral entities, and Hurt locker book also add the Bless amulet merit to improve this.<br /> Works well even against Frailties, vampire banes ecc...<br /> but it s a matter of luck if the creature has one of those vulnerabilities.<br /> Hurt locker book also add the option to build temporary charms using Occult, which gives bonus to stealth or damage improvement against a specific kind of creature","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T08:01:24-07:00","id":1465652,"title":"","content":"The best way to deal with widespread superstition is for it to frequently match local supernaturals Banes, Bans, etc.<br /> <br /> So it's not about making rules for the trinkets, but making rules for the supernatural creatures you'll put. Make your list of superstitions, then when you make a creature, chose one to three of those superstitions to work in some way, either directly or tangentially.<br /> <br /> As such, the superstitions will have been born of townsfolk interactions with the creatures and their experience with what works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T13:04:31-07:00","id":1465685,"title":"","content":"It sounds to me like this is the kind of game in which one wants something like the blue books Horrors rather than the full-fledged beings like the Kindred and changelings (and their adjacent creatures). A bit of a more subtle scale, doesn't need to come with the specifics of spirits, but can still use the Weakness rules for Bans and Banes that make things like special trinkets or ritual practices hold such creatures at bay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:23:14-07:00","id":1465803,"title":"","content":"\u201cDark Eras: the Sundered World\u201d also briefly mentioned common protection charms like this. IIRC it provided a blanket +2 to resist any supernatural powers. That\u2019d be simple to use.<br /> <br /> Having the charms provided a warded area would also be quite appropriate. Something like \u201cno supernatural being can cross or use its powers across this boundary\u201d. MtAw \u201cban (space 3)\u201d could be a good model for that [the rating of the barrier is withstood]. There were also some 1e powers that did something similar, like the Purified\u2019s warding siddhi in \u201cImmortals\u201d [I believe that required a roll similar to clash of wills each time whenever something tried cross].<br /> Wards against magic are a very classic bit of folk magic, but should come with quite a lot of restrictions. Like \u201ca boundary can only be made at a threshold (door, window, fireplace) - not large open areas\u201d. It may require someone specific create the boundary (a hedge witch or shaman). Or it might require several dozen specific rites on a regular basis (making the \u201cgeneral protection\u201d a result of exploiting numerous bans all layered together). Maybe all of those and a few more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:31:34-07:00","id":1465806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1465632-folk-magic?p=1465803#post1465803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cDark Eras: the Sundered World\u201d also briefly mentioned common protection charms like this. IIRC it provided a blanket +2 to resist any supernatural powers. That\u2019d be simple to use.<br /> <br /> Having the charms provided a warded area would also be quite appropriate. Something like \u201cno supernatural being can cross or use its powers across this boundary\u201d. MtAw \u201cban (space 3)\u201d could be a good model for that [the rating of the barrier is withstood]. There were also some 1e powers that did something similar, like the Purified\u2019s warding siddhi in \u201cImmortals\u201d [I believe that required a roll similar to clash of wills each time whenever something tried cross].<br /> Wards against magic are a very classic bit of folk magic, but should come with quite a lot of restrictions. Like \u201ca boundary can only be made at a threshold (door, window, fireplace) - not large open areas\u201d. It may require someone specific create the boundary (a hedge witch or shaman). Or it might require several dozen specific rites on a regular basis (making the \u201cgeneral protection\u201d a result of exploiting numerous bans all layered together). Maybe all of those and a few more.</div> </div> </div> </div>*idly waves over at Hurt Locker's Occult Skill section also having similiar things.*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T13:11:53-07:00","id":1465815,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the ideas thus far. The setting is a mix of CoD and legendry, so vampires are more or less as per VtR, while Fae are more out of folklore than Changeling. Based on the style of play for this particular setting and group, I'm consolidating powers -- one or two Merits coupled with Occult (local folklore) to build the talismans and wards. Adherence to folklore will keep most of locals safe, while visitors frequently upset the order of things and get hurt.<br /> <br /> Also, as suggested, the supernatural beings -- particularly spirits of various ilks -- have over time been moulded to the freedoms and restrictions of the local belief system. So a spirit may benefit from the daily observances of the locals (songs, offerings, and other remembrances) but be hemmed in by the bans induced by the protection prayers and amulets used by the same folk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","user":"Corrigan","date":". 11-02-2021, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T07:33:42-07:00","id":1466944,"title":"","content":"One thing to not overlook is that the building equipment rules might be a good thing to referance for charms and baubles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}